dropped the body
--
N5008 [class.mem.general]/7-8: a member function body is a complete-class
context, so a name used in it is looked up in the complete class
([basic.scope.class]) -- including a member typedef declared AFTER the
function (`action::copy' through the later `typedef imp::action action;').
The front end resolves the body before that typedef is visible ("could
not fully type-check 'copy'") and rejects the unit.  This is libc++'s
std::any: its members call `__call(_Action::_Copy, this)' ahead of the
private `typedef __any_imp::_Action _Action;' (any:198-275, six members
dropped in cpp17_libcxx_any, round-163 audit).  Header-free.
Pre-existing (round-162 snapshot bin51 fails the same way).
